// Relativization / partition-safety, negated-left `since` (the "session still
// open" idiom: no Logout since the last Login).
//
// A Read is permitted iff, for THIS principal, no Logout has occurred since
// its Login (within 1h). The event schema pins `callerPrincipal` universally,
// so the streak is evaluated over this principal's own events only.
//
// Differential pair for principal alice's Read at @3:
//   trace_1: alice Login @1, BOB Logout @2 (foreign), alice Read @3.
//   trace_2: alice Login @1,                          alice Read @3.
// Under key-local semantics bob's Logout cannot break alice's session, so the
// verdict is PERMIT in both traces. Under (incorrect) global semantics
// trace_1's bob Logout would fall in the (login, read] window and deny,
// diverging from trace_2. The rewrite makes them agree.
//
// Both Logout and Read events carry `input.user: "u"`, so the pinned
// `callerPrincipal` is the ONLY thing distinguishing alice's events from
// bob's — this is what the relativization must key on.

permit (
    principal,
    action == Drupe::Action::"Read",
    resource
)
when temporal {
    !Drupe::Action::"Logout"::request{ input.user: context.input.user }
    since within 1h
    Drupe::Action::"Login"::request{ input.user: context.input.user }
};
